# Stock /vendor/etc/init/android.hardware.light@2.0-service.waydroid.rc,
# neutered: the service still EXISTS by name but execs a no-op.
#
# WHY
#
# The shipped binary is a 15 KB stub. It registers
# android.hardware.light@2.0::ILight/default and discards every call -- it
# contains no file path strings at all, so it writes nowhere and Android's
# brightness slider has never moved anything. waydroid-sensord now serves that
# interface for real, mapping Android's 0..255 onto the host's
# /sys/class/backlight/intel_backlight (see sensors/Backlight.h).
#
# Both register the same name, and addService() overwrites, so the last one to
# register owns it. We always lose that race without this file:
# container_manager.py starts waydroid-sensord BEFORE lxc-start, so the guest
# stub is guaranteed to register second.
#
# WHY THE "interface" LINE IS DROPPED AND NOT KEPT
#
# This is the part 34-wifi-second-radio.md paid for the hard way with wificond.
# "disabled" alone was not enough there: it only means "do not auto-start at
# class main", and something still asked init to start the service on demand,
# which beat the host daemon every time. An `interface` line in a service block
# is exactly what lets init do that -- it is how init knows which service to
# start when a client waits for a HIDL name. Removing the line removes the
# trigger, so the three guards work together:
#
#   /system/bin/true  execs and exits immediately, so it can never reach
#                     addService() and can never take the name. It is a toybox
#                     symlink present in this image; checked, not assumed.
#   oneshot           init must NOT restart it when it exits. Without this the
#                     no-op respawns forever on a 5 s backoff.
#   disabled          not started at class hal either.
#
# "shutdown critical" goes with the real binary: it exists to let a lights HAL
# turn LEDs off during power-down, which /system/bin/true has no use for.
#
# EFFECT AND RISK
#
# waydroid-sensord owns ILight/default from whenever it starts. If it is not
# running, nothing serves the interface at all -- which is not a regression,
# because the stub it replaces did nothing anyway. The vendor VINTF manifest
# still declares the HAL; an undeclared-but-registered or declared-but-absent
# HAL is a VTS complaint, not a runtime failure.
#
# Reverting is deleting this file, which restores the stub and with it a
# brightness slider that moves nothing.
#
# Deploy to
# /var/lib/waydroid/overlay/vendor/etc/init/android.hardware.light@2.0-service.waydroid.rc
# (0644 root:root). Dropping the file in is NOT enough: the overlay lowerdir is
# already mounted, so it needs `systemctl restart waydroid-container.service`
# and a fresh session. See AGENTS.md and 32-wifi-stage3.md.
#
# Original for comparison:
#   artifacts/overlay/vendor/etc/init/android.hardware.light@2.0-service.waydroid.rc.orig
# Evidence and full reasoning: docs/37-brightness.md

service vendor.light-hal-2-0 /system/bin/true
    class hal
    user system
    group system graphics
    disabled
    oneshot
